NAME
    pkg-analyze - inspect an unpacked or packaged upstream software tree

SYNOPSIS
    pkg-analyze <directory>
    pkg-analyze <format> <artifact>

DESCRIPTION
    pkg-analyze inspects an existing directory or extracts an artifact into a
    temporary staging tree, reports candidate launch files and interactively
    allows candidates to be selected for optional probing.

    The dynamic probe is diagnostic only and is not a sandbox. Selected upstream
    programs run with the caller's user permissions. HOME and common XDG/state
    and temporary paths are redirected for the probe, while XDG_RUNTIME_DIR is
    preserved when present. The report shows observed pathname deltas.

    Temporary analysis state is created under the user sys pkg-analyze state
    area and is cleaned up on ordinary exit.

OPERANDS
    <directory>
        Existing directory to inspect directly.
    <format> <artifact>
        Artifact format and artifact consumed through the package extraction
        facility before analysis.

EXIT STATUS
    0   Analysis completed.
    2   Invalid invocation.
    Other non-zero status indicates input, extraction, scan, interaction or probe
        failure.
